%% Draft diagram. Application verification: NOT_RUN.
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as Player
    participant M as Memory owner
    participant C as Cutoff store
    participant D as Derived snapshot
    participant H as Raw history
    U->>M: Forget learned memory
    M->>C: Durably advance nondecreasing cutoff
    Note over M,C: Logical or epoch domain comparable with archives
    alt Durable write fails
        C-->>M: Failure
        M-->>U: Error, no success acknowledgement
    else Cutoff is durable
        C-->>M: Persisted cutoff
        M->>D: Discard derived memory
        D-->>M: Derived state cleared
        M-->>U: Forget acknowledged
    end
    Note over D,H: Raw history preserved, deletion is a separate action
    opt Later restart or rebuild
        M->>C: Load durable cutoff
        alt Missing validity due to corrupt or unreadable cutoff
            C-->>M: Invalid cutoff
            Note over M,H: Fail closed, do not relearn history
        else Valid cutoff
            C-->>M: Current cutoff
            M->>H: Read permitted sources newer than cutoff
            H-->>M: Eligible source evidence
            Note over M,H: Exclude same-granularity timestamps conservatively
            M->>D: Atomically replace versioned snapshot
        end
    end
